import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact — WasPetInsuranceWorthIt.com"
  description="How to reach WasPetInsuranceWorthIt.com — corrections to our pet insurance data, methodology questions, and privacy requests."
>
  <article class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
    <h1>Contact</h1>

    <p>
      WasPetInsuranceWorthIt.com is an independent consumer-research site. It exists to answer one
      question honestly: for a specific pet, with a specific breed, age, and vet-spending history,
      did pet insurance actually pay for itself? The calculator and the articles are built on
      published industry data — a 50,000-pet claims dataset, NAPHIA's annual industry report, and
      published procedure cost ranges — all of which are listed in full on the{' '}
      <a href="/about/">methodology page</a>. The site carries no affiliate links, takes no
      insurance company sponsorship, and does not sell leads.
    </p>

    <p>
      It is maintained by one person, not a company or an editorial team. That means replies can
      take a few days, but it also means corrections go straight to the person who can make them.
    </p>

    <p>Email is the only way to get in touch:</p>

    <p class="text-lg">
      <strong><!--email_off-->contact@waspetinsuranceworthit.com<!--/email_off--></strong>
    </p>

    <p>Messages worth sending:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Corrections to our pet insurance data.</strong> If a premium average, breed risk
        figure, waiting period, or exclusion rule on this site is wrong or out of date, say so.
        Please include the page and the source you are correcting it against — a carrier policy
        document, a NAPHIA figure, or a published study. Corrections get made and the page gets
        updated.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Methodology questions.</strong> If a calculator assumption does not make sense to
        you, or a number does not reconcile with what you were quoted, ask. The assumptions are
        documented, but documentation is not the same as being clear.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Privacy requests and bug reports.</strong> Anything about how the site handles
        data — see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> first — or anything on the site that
        is visibly broken.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      One thing this site cannot do: tell you which insurer to buy from, or review your specific
      policy. That is insurance advice, and nothing here is a substitute for it — see the{' '}
      <a href="/terms/">terms and disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
